{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0GW6", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-decent-locally-noetherian-sober}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a7839d23bf48e0dc6349546818aa2f7457c6239c3af9c433cafeb2e386faaef7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bd87dcd0173377419b475d399f1faf42b60452d2b26c8f8646517ada8f5f65a7", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a decent, locally Noetherian algebraic stack.\nThen <MATH_0002> is a sober locally Noetherian topological space.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9cffb9c3a8c586e38ee77ffe61e4d42fa56a0b6f1245b1aff82e482946faa437", "unit_id": "tag:0GW8:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0GW6", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0002": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0003": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-Noetherian-topology}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-kolmogorov}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-locally-Noetherian-quasi-sober}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{topology-definition-generic-point}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:78d798a27a859807649d11bf3cdb599424a69be5322439315e5fc25340554929", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2d02df691901475c4ee77de3734993f86cebc4053641c780a4d4fc798379f5ab", "source_text": "By Lemma <REF_0001> the topological space <MATH_0001>\nis locally Noetherian. By Lemma <REF_0002> the topological space\n<MATH_0002> is Kolmogorov. By\nLemma <REF_0003> the topological space\n<MATH_0003> is quasi-sober. This finishes the proof, see\nTopology, Definition <REF_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:17619cfe184b1c905eaaea142bc60f4bb5071ddb66f825b379b639980c1a0086", "unit_id": "tag:0GW8:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proposition", "parent_tag": "0GW6", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proposition}\n\\label{proposition-decent-sober}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proposition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:963246726c97a749366ee50690aed0a04e45fab35fbde9fa2f2f54c2eed1992b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4ee095b93c9dc08aeca9500bec1d81bcdf0c652edc6f12cd731112a9bf4610bd", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a decent algebraic stack such that\n<MATH_0002> is quasi-compact.\nThen <MATH_0003> is sober.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5f025ea522b90540388db1210df4ff0258695beed0c604ece5188e88b56f610e", "unit_id": "tag:0GW9:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0GW6", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0002": "$T \\subset |\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0003": "$T$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\subset \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0005": "$T$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0014": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0015": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{U} \\subset \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0017": "$|\\mathcal{U}| \\subset |\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0018": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0019": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to X$", "MATH_0020": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0021": "$X$", "MATH_0022": "$|\\mathcal{X}| \\cong |X|$", "MATH_0023": "$X$", "MATH_0024": "$|X|$", "MATH_0025": "$X$", "MATH_0026": "$|\\mathcal{X}| = |X|$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-kolmogorov}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{stacks-properties-definition-reduced-induced-stack}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-representable-decent}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-monomorphism-cartesian-square-inertia}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-quasi-compact}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{proposition-open-stratum}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{lemma-gerbe-bijection-points}", "REF_0008": "\\ref{lemma-gerbe-decent}", "REF_0009": "\\ref{decent-spaces-proposition-reasonable-sober}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fc13f2a3d2db76147c0607bd7ec1fef1129f219b4dfb51b5e79a525b2e22342a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a03d1a56d1ea1fda3bcd3d9ff0dae743111e831e5a6538786b29e92526fd07c7", "source_text": "By Lemma <REF_0001> we know that <MATH_0001> is Kolmogorov\n(in fact we will reprove this).\nLet <MATH_0002> be an irreducible closed subset.\nWe have to show <MATH_0003> has a generic point.\nLet <MATH_0004> be the reduced induced\nclosed substack corresponding to <MATH_0005>, see Properties of Stacks, Definition\n<REF_0002>.\nSince <MATH_0006> is a closed immersion,\nwe see that <MATH_0007> is a decent algebraic stack, see\nLemma <REF_0003>.\nAlso, the morphism <MATH_0008>\nis the base change of <MATH_0009>\n(Lemma <REF_0004>).\nHence <MATH_0010> is quasi-compact\n(Lemma <REF_0005>).\nThus we reduce to the case discussed in the next paragraph.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nAssume <MATH_0011> is decent,\n<MATH_0012> is quasi-compact,\n<MATH_0013> is reduced, and <MATH_0014> irreducible.\nWe have to show <MATH_0015> has a generic point.\nBy Proposition <REF_0006>.\nthere exists a dense open substack <MATH_0016>\nwhich is a gerbe. In other words, <MATH_0017>\nis open dense. Thus we may assume that <MATH_0018> is a gerbe\nin addition to all the other properties.\nSay <MATH_0019> turns <MATH_0020> into a gerbe over the\nalgebraic space <MATH_0021>. Then <MATH_0022> by\nLemma <REF_0007>.\nIn particular, <MATH_0023> is quasi-compact and <MATH_0024> is irreducible.\nAlso, by Lemma <REF_0008>\nwe see that <MATH_0025> is a decent algebraic space.\nThen <MATH_0026> is sober by\nDecent Spaces, Proposition <REF_0009>\nand hence has a (unique) generic point.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bc30ab5703b7095e383a7705580df6d1df8c61d4fe1b2dbe999bdfadc56540cc", "unit_id": "tag:0GW9:proof"}
